Task 1: Install Argo CD on Kubernetes
Subtask 1.1: Install Docker
First, we need to install Docker as our container runtime.

# Update the package index
sudo apt update

# Install required packages
sudo apt install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificates curl gnupg lsb-release

# Add Docker's official GPG key
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/docker-archive-keyring.gpg

# Set up the stable repository
echo "deb [arch=amd64 signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/docker-archive-keyring.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu $(lsb_release -cs) stable" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list > /dev/null

# Update package index again
sudo apt update

# Install Docker Engine
sudo apt install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io

# Add current user to docker group
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER

# Start and enable Docker service
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker
Log out and log back in for the group changes to take effect, or run:

newgrp docker
Verify Docker installation:

docker --version
docker run hello-world
Subtask 1.2: Install kubectl
Install the Kubernetes command-line tool:

# Download the latest kubectl binary
curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"

# Make kubectl executable
chmod +x kubectl

# Move kubectl to system PATH
sudo mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/

# Verify installation
kubectl version --client
Subtask 1.3: Install and Start Minikube
Install Minikube to create a local Kubernetes cluster:

# Download Minikube binary
curl -LO https://storage.googleapis.com/minikube/releases/latest/minikube-linux-amd64

# Install Minikube
sudo install minikube-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/minikube

# Start Minikube cluster
minikube start --driver=docker

# Verify cluster is running
kubectl cluster-info
kubectl get nodes
Subtask 1.4: Create Argo CD Namespace
Create a dedicated namespace for Argo CD:

# Create the argocd namespace
kubectl create namespace argocd

# Verify namespace creation
kubectl get namespaces
Subtask 1.5: Install Argo CD
Install Argo CD using the official installation manifest:

# Apply the Argo CD installation manifest
kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml

# Wait for all pods to be ready (this may take a few minutes)
kubectl wait --for=condition=available --timeout=600s deployment/argocd-server -n argocd

# Verify all Argo CD components are running
kubectl get pods -n argocd
You should see several pods running, including:

argocd-application-controller
argocd-applicationset-controller
argocd-dex-server
argocd-notifications-controller
argocd-redis
argocd-repo-server
argocd-server
Task 2: Configure API Server and Repository Server
Subtask 2.1: Configure API Server for External Access
By default, the Argo CD API server is not exposed externally. We'll configure it for access:

# Patch the argocd-server service to use NodePort
kubectl patch svc argocd-server -n argocd -p '{"spec":{"type":"NodePort"}}'

# Get the NodePort assigned
kubectl get svc argocd-server -n argocd
Alternative method using port forwarding (recommended for this lab):

# Forward local port 8080 to argocd-server service port 443
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 &
Subtask 2.2: Retrieve Admin Password
Get the initial admin password for Argo CD:

# Get the initial admin password
kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d && echo

# Store the password in a variable for later use
ARGOCD_PASSWORD=$(kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d)
echo "Admin password: $ARGOCD_PASSWORD"
Subtask 2.3: Install Argo CD CLI
Install the Argo CD command-line interface:

# Download the latest Argo CD CLI
curl -sSL -o argocd-linux-amd64 https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-amd64

# Make it executable
chmod +x argocd-linux-amd64

# Move to system PATH
sudo mv argocd-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/argocd

# Verify installation
argocd version --client
Subtask 2.4: Login to Argo CD
Login to Argo CD using the CLI:

# Login to Argo CD (skip TLS verification for local setup)
argocd login localhost:8080 --username admin --password $ARGOCD_PASSWORD --insecure

# Verify login
argocd account get-user-info
Subtask 2.5: Configure Repository Server
Configure the repository server to work with Git repositories:

# Check current repository server configuration
kubectl get deployment argocd-repo-server -n argocd -o yaml | grep -A 10 -B 10 "image:"

# Verify repository server is running
kubectl get pods -n argocd -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-repo-server
Create a configuration file to customize repository server settings:

# Create a ConfigMap for repository server configuration
cat <<EOF > repo-server-config.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: argocd-repo-server-config
  namespace: argocd
data:
  repositories: |
    - type: git
      url: https://github.com/argoproj/argocd-example-apps.git
  repository.credentials: |
    - url: https://github.com/argoproj
      passwordSecret:
        name: github-secret
        key: password
      usernameSecret:
        name: github-secret
        key: username
EOF

# Apply the configuration
kubectl apply -f repo-server-config.yaml
Subtask 2.6: Verify Argo CD Installation
Perform comprehensive verification of the Argo CD installation:

# Check all Argo CD services
kubectl get svc -n argocd

# Check all Argo CD deployments
kubectl get deployments -n argocd

# Check Argo CD server logs
kubectl logs deployment/argocd-server -n argocd --tail=20

# Check repository server logs
kubectl logs deployment/argocd-repo-server -n argocd --tail=20

# List all Argo CD applications (should be empty initially)
argocd app list
Subtask 2.7: Access Argo CD Web Interface
Access the Argo CD web interface to verify the installation:

# Get the Minikube IP
minikube ip

# If using port forwarding, the web interface is available at:
echo "Argo CD Web Interface: https://localhost:8080"
echo "Username: admin"
echo "Password: $ARGOCD_PASSWORD"
Note: Since we're using port forwarding, you can access the web interface at https://localhost:8080. Accept the self-signed certificate warning in your browser.

Subtask 2.8: Create a Test Application
Create a simple test application to verify Argo CD functionality:

# Create a test application using the CLI
argocd app create guestbook \
  --repo https://github.com/argoproj/argocd-example-apps.git \
  --path guestbook \
  --dest-server https://kubernetes.default.svc \
  --dest-namespace default

# List applications to verify creation
argocd app list

# Get application details
argocd app get guestbook

# Sync the application
argocd app sync guestbook

# Check application status
argocd app get guestbook
Verify the application deployment in Kubernetes:

# Check if guestbook pods are running
kubectl get pods -l app=guestbook-ui

# Check guestbook service
kubectl get svc guestbook-ui

# Check all resources created by the application
kubectl get all -l app.kubernetes.io/instance=guestbook
Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: Pods stuck in Pending state

# Check node resources
kubectl describe nodes
kubectl top nodes

# Check pod events
kubectl describe pod <pod-name> -n argocd
Issue 2: Cannot access Argo CD web interface

# Verify port forwarding is active
ps aux | grep kubectl

# Restart port forwarding if needed
pkill -f "kubectl port-forward"
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 &
Issue 3: Authentication issues

# Reset admin password
kubectl -n argocd patch secret argocd-secret -p '{"data":{"admin.password":null,"admin.passwordMtime":null}}'
kubectl -n argocd scale deployment argocd-server --replicas=0
kubectl -n argocd scale deployment argocd-server --replicas=1

# Get new password
kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d
Issue 4: Repository server connection problems

# Check repository server logs
kubectl logs deployment/argocd-repo-server -n argocd

# Verify network connectivity
kubectl exec -it deployment/argocd-repo-server -n argocd -- nslookup github.com
